    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter August 24th with a clear hierarchy in offensive priority, headlined by **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (82.13) and **Junior Caminero** (76.13). **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is our premier start, leveraging an elite matchup against Merrill Kelly; the combination of a high-ceiling platoon advantage and the top spot in the order maximizes his sprint speed utility\u2014our highest priority in this 5x5 format. Meanwhile, **Junior Caminero** faces Framber Valdez, and while facing a southpaw is usually a friction point, the park factors and favorable batting order position boost his efficiency into the elite tier. Both players are positioned to carry our scoring against suspect pitching staffs today.\n\nMid-tier reliability is anchored by **Lars Nootbaar** (60.62), who benefits from a significant boost due to his favorable platoon matchup against Kevin Gausman, climbing above the 60-point threshold to secure a spot in the outfield. Conversely, we are keeping a close watch on **Trea Turner** (51.35) and **Kyle Schwarber** (50.87); both players face Logan Gilbert, an elite arm whose presence suppresses their baseline projections. While their order positions keep them start-worthy, they are playing near the floor of our efficiency requirements. **Dillon Dingler** (37.53) remains our most difficult bench decision, ultimately excluded because his platoon disadvantage against Rasmussen forces his efficiency score well below our 40-point organizational threshold, preserving game caps for more favorable future matchups. With **Yordan Alvarez**, **Christian Yelich**, and **Kazuma Okamoto** all sidelined by team off-days, our depth is tested, but the active roster remains optimized to exploit the specific starting pitcher weaknesses presented on today's slate.",
